  "lineage": "Trapezoidal 72-81-string plucked box zither central to the Arab takht and Ottoman fasil from the 19th century, standardized with the mandal lever system in early-20th-century Cairo and Istanbul workshops and codified by players such as Muhammad al-Aqqad, Abraham Salman and Ruhi Ayangil, marked by tortoise-shell plectrum rings, dense tremolo and rapid descending runs, mid-phrase mandal shifts that retune quarter-tone degrees for maqam modulation, and unmetered taqsim alternating with heterophonic ensemble accompaniment.",
